5227f"} {"question" "q-119184" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following diagrams gives the slope field at the points indicated for the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=1-x?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040080/state.json" "file_sha256" "596ecaa0bb329d9f3a0070638fa5ac6148b88f020090b38a93ff812372b5227f"} {"question" "q-119184" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We have to sketch the slope field at the points $(-2,2),(-2,-1)$ and $(2,-2).$\n\nTo sketch the slope field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the right-hand side of the differential equation.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(-2,2)}=1-(-2)=3, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(-2,-1)}=1-(-2)=3, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(2,-2)}=1-2=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting up our points and drawing our line segments, we get the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040080/assets/911af9ca268f5f4c9cbac7b9c063eae54defce6d99dfadef609892b93ad58ae4.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040080/state.json" "file_sha256" "596ecaa0bb329d9f3a0070638fa5ac6148b88f020090b38a93ff812372b5227f"} {"question" "q-119184" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040080/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "07cec2c49e52c7e72c68f9a1da0765bb9729da52389ca343617ace328a4f0b25"} {"question" "q-119184" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/re